  m_Name: motion-capture
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: GameTerms.Runtime::GameTerms.GlossaryTermAsset
  data:
    Id: motion-capture
    Term: Motion Capture
    Abbreviation: mocap
    Category: 3
    Difficulty: 1
    ShortDefinition: Recording real performer movement and transferring it onto a
      digital character.
    SimpleExplanation: Capture a person's motion with sensors or cameras and apply
      it to a 3D character.
    WhyItMatters: Mo-cap accelerates realistic animation production for cinematic
      and gameplay needs.
    Example: A fight choreography recorded on a stage and cleaned for an in-game
      finisher.
    CommonMistake: Shipping raw capture without cleanup, leaving foot slides and
      noise.
    PracticePrompt: Plan a short capture shot list with cleanup and retargeting steps.
    GameUses:
    - Cinematics
    - Sports games
    - Realistic combat
    RelatedTermIds:
    - retargeting
    - keyframe-animation
    - rigging
    Tags:
    - animation
    - pipeline
    - performance
    Synonyms:
    - mo-cap
    CodeExample: 
